<script lang="ts">
	import { examples } from '../../utils/examples'

	const markdown = signal('## Release notes\n\nWrite **here** or switch to code mode.\n\n- Without editing, the text does not change.\n- Only the block you touch is rewritten.\n')
	const mode = signal<'visual' | 'code'>('visual')
</script>

<template>
	<DocsPage
		locale="en"
		title="Markdown editor"
		description="UIMarkdownEditor edits Markdown with Crepe and a code mode, and keeps the bytes of what you do not touch."
	>
		<p>
			<code>UIMarkdownEditor</code>
			lives in its own module,
			<code>@meekojs/ui/editor</code>
			, because Crepe weighs 347 KB of gzipped JS: inside the main module it would be a chunk of every site. The JavaScript of Crepe loads in the browser, when the component mounts, and never enters the server bundle. Until then, the HTML of the server paints a placeholder with the final height.
		</p>
		<h2 id="setup">Setup</h2>
		<p>
			Crepe and CodeMirror are optional dependencies of
			<code>@meekojs/ui</code>
			: an application without the module does not install them.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="meeko.config.ts"
			bind:code="examples.editorConfig"
		/>
		<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
		<UIMarkdownEditor
			label="Content"
			model="markdown"
			model:mode="mode"
		/>
		<p
			id="editor-status"
			class="docs-status"
			role="status"
		>
			{mode.value === 'code' ? 'Code' : 'Visual'} mode: {markdown.value.length} characters.
		</p>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.editor" />
		<h2 id="saving">Block-level saving</h2>
		<p>Crepe serializes a document in its own format, so saving its output would rewrite tables and blank lines nobody touched. That is why the model only changes with a real edit, and then it keeps the bytes of the original outside the edited blocks.</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				Without editing,
				<code>model</code>
				stays the received text, byte by byte. Typing and undoing too.
			</li>
			<li>An edited block comes out of Crepe. A list is one block.</li>
			<li>The frontmatter never reaches Crepe: it is kept as it is.</li>
			<li>The event waits for a pause while typing, and comes early when leaving the editor, before a click on «save» reads the model.</li>
			<li>If a document does not match its serialization block by block, it opens in code mode with a notice.</li>
		</ul>
		<h2 id="api">API</h2>
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIMarkdownEditor props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'model', type: 'Signal<string>', description: 'The text. If the parent writes another one, the editor starts over with it.' },
				{ name: 'model:mode', type: 'Signal<visual | code>', default: 'visual', description: 'The mode.' },
				{ name: 'label', type: 'string', description: 'Required. Visible label and accessible name.' },
				{ name: 'id', type: 'string', description: 'id of the text area of the code mode.' },
				{ name: 'readonly', type: 'boolean', default: 'false', description: 'It can be read and selected, but not changed.' },
				{ name: 'disabled', type: 'boolean', default: 'false', description: 'Like readonly, and it also looks disabled.' },
				{ name: 'describedBy', type: 'string', description: 'id of the text that describes it.' },
				{ name: 'placeholder', type: 'string', description: 'Text of the empty document.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Class of the root.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			The
			<code>tools</code>
			snippet goes in the bar, between the label and the switcher. The height is set with
			<code>--ui-markdown-editor-height</code>
			and the content scrolls inside. Its texts, also those of the menus of Crepe, are in
			<code>ui.messages.&lt;language&gt;.markdownEditor</code>
			.
			<code>splitMarkdownSource</code>
			and
			<code>createMarkdownSplicer</code>
			are exported from
			<code>@meekojs/ui/editor</code>
			, without Crepe.
		</p>
	</DocsPage>
</template>
